          "source": "def-admissible-regular-parametrized-surface-patch",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "A **compact Jordan parameter region** is a compact Jordan measurable set $D\\subseteq\\mathbb R^2$ that is the closure of its nonempty connected interior $D^\\circ$ ([[def-riemann-integral-over-a-jordan-set]], [[def-metric-interior-closure-boundary]]). Its boundary has content zero ([[thm-jordan-boundary-criterion]]).\n\nA regular parametrized surface patch is the image of a $C^1$ map from a compact Jordan parameter region whose parameter cross product is nonzero on the region's interior and for which no interior parameter point shares its image with a distinct point of the whole region. Seam identifications and rank failures may occur only on the boundary. Here $C^1$ is the Euclidean componentwise class of [[def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms]]. More precisely, the parametrization $\\varphi$ is defined on an open neighbourhood of $D$, $\\varphi_u\\times\\varphi_v\\ne0$ on $D^\\circ$, and no point of $D^\\circ$ has the same image as a distinct point of $D$. The chosen pair $(D,\\varphi)$ is part of the patch data.",
