          "quote": "Let $n\\ge1$, let $U\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$ be open, let $g:U\\to\\mathbb R^n$ be injective and $C^1$, and suppose $Dg(x)$ is invertible for every $x\\in U$. Let $K\\subseteq U$ be compact and Jordan measurable. For a bounded function $f:g(K)\\to\\mathbb R$, the following are equivalent:\n\n1. $f$ is Riemann integrable on $g(K)$;\n2. $x\\mapsto f(g(x))|\\det Dg(x)|$ is Riemann integrable on $K$.\n\nWhen either condition holds,\n$$\\int_{g(K)}f(y)\\,dy=\\int_K f(g(x))|\\det Dg(x)|\\,dx.$$",
